  <metadata>
    <name>S07 The blue-stone coast to Ende</name>
    <desc>Section 07 of the Flores Race traverse: Crossing the island's narrow waist. 106.6 km, +2093 m / -2054 m, starts at km 798 of the course.</desc>
    <link href="https://github.com/technicaloutdoor/Flores-Race"><text>Flores Race Planner</text></link>
    <time>2026-09-05T06:27:58Z</time>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="-8.575600" lon="121.280700">
    <ele>36.4</ele>
    <name>Mbay</name>
    <desc>km 0.0 | kind: town | resupply: full | water: reliable | sleep: hotel -- Administrative capital of Nagekeo Regency, on the Aesesa coastal plain (the largest rice-growing lowland on Flores), north coast. Desk position corrected ~17.3 km from an earlier unverified placement to the Civic Center </desc>
    <sym>City (Medium)</sym>
    <type>anchor/town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.786389" lon="121.391667">
    <ele>19.0</ele>
    <name>Nangaroro</name>
    <desc>km 55.5 | kind: village | resupply: basic | water: unreliable | sleep: homestay -- South-coast district of Nagekeo Regency bordering Ende; farming and fishing villages (Tonggo etc.), grey-stone beaches; an alternative south-coast crossing from Boawae/Mbay toward Ende.</desc>
    <sym>Residence</sym>
    <type>anchor/village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.797553" lon="121.451672">
    <ele>4.3</ele>
    <name>Penggajawa</name>
    <desc>km 66.4 | kind: village | resupply: minimal | water: unreliable | sleep: none | position approximate -- Coastal village in Nangapanda district, Ende Regency, on the Blue Stone (Batu Biru) beach, ~25 km west of Ende on the Bajawa-Ende road.</desc>
    <sym>Residence</sym>
    <type>anchor/village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.838100" lon="121.656150">
    <ele>68.7</ele>
    <name>Ende</name>
    <desc>km 106.6 | kind: town | resupply: full | water: reliable | sleep: hotel -- Largest town of central Flores, capital of Ende Regency, on the south coast under Iya volcano; full resupply, hospital, airport, Sukarno's 1934-38 exile town. Natural Earth's populated-place point for Ende sits 2.81 km s</desc>
    <sym>City (Medium)</sym>
    <type>anchor/town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.849170" lon="121.660560">
    <ele>13.0</ele>
    <name>H. Hasan Aroeboesman Airport</name>
    <desc>[resupply] Ende's airport (IATA ENE), ~2 km southeast of the town centre; scheduled flights to Kupang, Bali and other Flores towns, and the region's main air-evacuation point.</desc>
    <sym>Airport</sym>
    <type>poi/airport</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.838100" lon="121.656150">
    <ele>68.7</ele>
    <name>Ende</name>
    <desc>[resupply] Capital of Ende Regency and the largest town of central Flores, on the south coast under Iya volcano; full resupply, hospital, airport, and the town where Sukarno was exiled 1934-38.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/heritage</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.846900" lon="121.662900">
    <ele>15.5</ele>
    <name>Bung Karno Contemplation Park</name>
    <desc>[highlight] A seafront park in Ende where Sukarno is said to have contemplated the five principles of Pancasila under a breadfruit tree during his 1934-38 exile; the current tree (planted 1980) has five branches.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/heritage</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.797553" lon="121.451672">
    <ele>4.3</ele>
    <name>Penggajawa Blue Stone Beach</name>
    <desc>[highlight] A pebble beach in Penggajawa village, Nangapanda district, Ende Regency, ~25 km west of Ende; smooth blue-turquoise volcanic pebbles washed up from old lava flows, a classic overland-route photo stop.</desc>
    <sym>Beach</sym>
    <type>poi/beach</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.840767" lon="121.644439">
    <ele>19.5</ele>
    <name>Bung Karno's Exile House</name>
    <desc>[highlight] The house on Jalan Perwira, Ende, where Sukarno lived during his 1934-38 exile under the Dutch colonial government; a museum of his belongings since 1954.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/heritage</type>
  </wpt>
